# Project rules for Claude

<!-- Copy to the repo root as CLAUDE.md and fill in. Keep it short: rules, not docs. -->

## Project
- Platform / stack: <iOS SwiftUI | Android Compose | Flutter>, min OS <x>
- Architecture: <Clean Architecture + MVI / MVVM …>; feature folders: <path>
- Design system module: <path> — always reuse its tokens and components
- Source of truth: business logic & API = <Flutter repo path>; UI = <Figma link>

## Build & run
- Build: `<command>`
- Run on simulator/emulator: `<command>`
- Tests: `<command>`

## Git
- Never commit or push on `main` / `develop` — create `feature/<TICKET>-<slug>`.
- Commit subject: `<TICKET-123> short summary`
- Ask before every push, merge request or release.

## Working style
- Every UI change goes to iOS AND Android in the same pass.
- Analyse the Flutter source fully before porting; port 1:1, never approximate.
- Strings only through localization (<languages>).
- Files that must never be committed: <debug hacks, local configs>

## Intentional deviations from Flutter
- <component>: <what differs and why — approved by whom/when>
